       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common regimen for mild to moderate pain\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), often used for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, which is sometimes used for arthritis\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
